(4096754, 587922, 68546, '<td valign="top">I find the combination of colours and textures remove the key quality that made the ribbon shot so great and that''s its pure simplicity. It was all about the composition and the touch of colour. This entry has a lot more distractions and so is visually less striking. Technically very good though with even lighting and good focus</td>', 'I find the combination of colours and textures remove the key quality that made the ribbon shot so great and that''s its pure simplicity. It was all about the composition and the touch of colour. This entry has a lot more distractions and so is visually less striking. Technically very good though with even lighting and good focus', '2007-09-17 15:17:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(4096762, 587917, 68546, '<td valign="top">And you managed to do this one in Advanced editing as well!! Very good entry, funny as well as creative and well lit. Great work</td>', 'And you managed to do this one in Advanced editing as well!! Very good entry, funny as well as creative and well lit. Great work', '2007-09-17 15:21:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(4096764, 587328, 68947, '<td valign="top">Lovely shot!  <br/> <br/>One day, the Pixie Dust Faeries breezed through a field of flowers, sprinkling Blue Magic on all the flowers in the land.  All of the flowers turned a lovely shade of blue.  However, there were these one group of flowers that simply refused to turn blue!  Their yellow heads stood out amongst all of the other blue flowers, standing proud and tall.  Their bright yellow shone out from a sea of blue, making them more special than the rest.  And, try as they may, the Faeries just simply could not turn these flowers into the shade of blue that all of the others had turned.  They were simply far too resilient to ever conform.<br/> <br/>And, so they stand today.....the yellow flowers in a blue world, bringing happy smiles to all that have the luck to gaze upon their beauty.  Some will say that they do not fit in.  Others will say.....they stand out.  I, personally, believe that they have chosen to "stand out" and be themselves with will and determination because afterall, they are beautiful and they have learned to recognize that fitting in, doesn''t necessarily mean "beauty"!  <br/> <br/>Ode To The "Michelle Flower" from a Pea Pod Mate!</td>', 'Lovely shot!   One day, the Pixie Dust Faeries breezed through a field of flowers, sprinkling Blue Magic on all the flowers in the land.  All of the flowers turned a lovely shade of blue.  However, there were these one group of flowers that simply refused to turn blue!  Their yellow heads stood out amongst all of the other blue flowers, standing proud and tall.  Their bright yellow shone out from a sea of blue, making them more special than the rest.  And, try as they may, the Faeries just simply could not turn these flowers into the shade of blue that all of the others had turned.  They were simply far too resilient to ever conform. And, so they stand today.....the yellow flowers in a blue world, bringing happy smiles to all that have the luck to gaze upon their beauty.  Some will say that they do not fit in.  Others will say.....they stand out.  I, personally, believe that they have chosen to "stand out" and be themselves with will and determination because afterall, they are beautiful and they have learned to recognize that fitting in, doesn''t necessarily mean "beauty"!   Ode To The "Michelle Flower" from a Pea Pod Mate!', '2007-09-17 15:22:40.000000', NULL, 1),
