(4112160, 585034, 39184, '<td valign="top">In response to your comment "<i>...but I hope he likes it!</i>", I have to say that I absolutely LOVE IT!!!  I am honored and very flattered that you chose Rainforest to pay tribute to.  Thank you.<br/> <br/>No, you weren''t able to find a leaf with any red in it, but the detail that you got in the leaf structure is amazingly good and has a 3D look to it.  It seems that you were actually able to get some shadows around the veins of the leaf.<br/> <br/>Everything, from the position of the frog, the scale of the frog versus the leaf, the crop around the leaf so that the veins at the top exit the image at almost the exact same place as my crop, to even the border around the image has been very well recreated.  You definitely took some time to pay attention to the details and recreate them here.  <i>edit to add---&gt;</i>  I just noticed that you even found the original frog silhouette.  I thought that you probably printed out Rainforest and cut out the frog from that.  But no, the silhouette was cut out in a slightly different way and I can tell that it was as difficult for you as it was for me making clean cuts around the small details.<br/> <br/>I am wondering if it was difficult to pull this off since it took me so many attempts and many retakes to overcome the various problems that I encountered, or were you able to accomplish this detailed reproduction easily by following my comments as to how I was finally able to make it?  Did you find an easier way of cutting out the frog?  What was your setup and did you also tape the leaf to glass for the backlighting?  It would be very interesting to hear your account of how you created this great image.<br/> <br/>Again, very nicely done with so much attention paid to the details of the original.  It would have been nice to see this on the front page again but a top 5 finsh is a great accomplishment.  Thank you for paying tribute to one of my images.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-09-24 09:48:18.</i></td>', 'In response to your comment "...but I hope he likes it!", I have to say that I absolutely LOVE IT!!!  I am honored and very flattered that you chose Rainforest to pay tribute to.  Thank you. No, you weren''t able to find a leaf with any red in it, but the detail that you got in the leaf structure is amazingly good and has a 3D look to it.  It seems that you were actually able to get some shadows around the veins of the leaf. Everything, from the position of the frog, the scale of the frog versus the leaf, the crop around the leaf so that the veins at the top exit the image at almost the exact same place as my crop, to even the border around the image has been very well recreated.  You definitely took some time to pay attention to the details and recreate them here.  edit to add--->  I just noticed that you even found the original frog silhouette.  I thought that you probably printed out Rainforest and cut out the frog from that.  But no, the silhouette was cut out in a slightly different way and I can tell that it was as difficult for you as it was for me making clean cuts around the small details. I am wondering if it was difficult to pull this off since it took me so many attempts and many retakes to overcome the various problems that I encountered, or were you able to accomplish this detailed reproduction easily by following my comments as to how I was finally able to make it?  Did you find an easier way of cutting out the frog?  What was your setup and did you also tape the leaf to glass for the backlighting?  It would be very interesting to hear your account of how you created this great image. Again, very nicely done with so much attention paid to the details of the original.  It would have been nice to see this on the front page again but a top 5 finsh is a great accomplishment.  Thank you for paying tribute to one of my images.', '2007-09-24 10:37:37.000000', '2007-09-24 10:48:18.000000', 0),
