(4117388, 587355, 84621, '<td valign="top">The difference, to me, is that whereas the other two pix you cite lead the eye to a visible vanishing point, yours has a hook to the left in the far distance, which is reinforced by the clouds on the horizon. Adds mystery. To me it''s better because of that. Makes you want to ride on down the road to find out what''s there. With the dsidwell and wavelength pix, you''re quite happy to sit where you are and admire the view. <br/> <br/>A fine pic.</td>', 'The difference, to me, is that whereas the other two pix you cite lead the eye to a visible vanishing point, yours has a hook to the left in the far distance, which is reinforced by the clouds on the horizon. Adds mystery. To me it''s better because of that. Makes you want to ride on down the road to find out what''s there. With the dsidwell and wavelength pix, you''re quite happy to sit where you are and admire the view.  A fine pic.', '2007-09-26 12:39:47.000000', NULL, 0),
